  "question": "Differentiate between scalar and vector quantities with examples.",
  "gold_answer": "# Introduction\n\n---\n\n## Definition\n\nPhysical quantities in classical mechanics are categorized into two structural classes based on their directional dependence properties.\n\nA scalar quantity is a physical property that is completely described by its magnitude (a numerical value with its matching measurement unit) without any directional tracking context.\n\nA vector quantity is a physical property that requires both a defined magnitude and a clear spatial direction descriptor to be fully specified.\n\n---\n\n## Comparison Matrix\n\n| Characteristics | Scalar Quantities | Vector Quantities |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Components** | Possess magnitude descriptors exclusively. | Require both magnitude and direction vectors. |\n| **Mathematical Logic** | Combine via basic algebraic addition. | Require vector addition laws (triangle law). |\n| **Graphic Profile** | Represented simply by static numbers. | Represented graphically by directed straight arrows. |\n\n---\n\n## Real-world Examples\n\n* **Scalar Class:** Speed ($50 \\text{ km/h}$), mass ($10 \\text{ kg}$), temperature ($37^\\circ\\text{C}$), and time interval ($12 \\text{ s}$).\n* **Vector Class:** Velocity ($50 \\text{ km/h due North}$), weight ($98 \\text{ N downward}$), and force ($15 \\text{ N applied East}$).\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nScalars maintain total independence from spatial alignment changes, while vectors update their identity if either their magnitude scales or their orientation axes shift.",
  "candidate_response": "<div class=\"tutor-response\">\n\n# Scalar vs Vector Quantities\n\n<div class=\"section-grid\">\n\n<div class=\"concept-card full-width\">\n<div class=\"card-header intro-header\">\n<span class=\"card-icon\">📖</span>\n<span class=\"card-title\">Overview</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\nPhysical quantities in physics are classified into two fundamental categories based on whether they require a <strong>direction</strong> to be fully described. Understanding this distinction is foundational to all of classical mechanics.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<div class=\"section-grid two-col\">\n\n<div class=\"concept-card\">\n<div class=\"card-header scalar-header\">\n<span class=\"card-icon\">🔢</span>\n<span class=\"card-title\">Scalar Quantity</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<p>A quantity that is <strong>completely described by magnitude alone</strong> — no direction is needed.</p>\n\n<div class=\"property-list\">\n<div class=\"property-item\">\n<span class=\"property-label\">Representation</span>\n<span class=\"property-value\">Simple number with unit</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"property-item\">\n<span class=\"property-label\">Direction</span>\n<span class=\"property-value\">❌ Not required</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"property-item\">\n<span class=\"property-label\">Algebra</span>\n<span class=\"property-value\">Ordinary arithmetic</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"example-box scalar-example\">\n<div class=\"example-title\">Examples</div>\n<div class=\"example-tags\">\n<span class=\"tag\">Mass — 5 kg</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Temperature — 37°C</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Speed — 60 km/h</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Energy — 200 J</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Time — 10 s</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Distance — 100 m</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"concept-card\">\n<div class=\"card-header vector-header\">\n<span class=\"card-icon\">➡️</span>\n<span class=\"card-title\">Vector Quantity</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<p>A quantity that requires both <strong>magnitude AND direction</strong> for complete description.</p>\n\n<div class=\"property-list\">\n<div class=\"property-item\">\n<span class=\"property-label\">Representation</span>\n<span class=\"property-value\">Arrow or bold symbol <strong>F</strong></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"property-item\">\n<span class=\"property-label\">Direction</span>\n<span class=\"property-value\">✅ Essential</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"property-item\">\n<span class=\"property-label\">Algebra</span>\n<span class=\"property-value\">Vector addition rules</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"example-box vector-example\">\n<div class=\"example-title\">Examples</div>\n<div class=\"example-tags\">\n<span class=\"tag\">Force — 10 N East</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Velocity — 60 km/h North</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Displacement — 5 m upward</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Acceleration — 9.8 m/s² down</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Momentum — 20 kg·m/s</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Electric Field</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<div class=\"formula-card\">\n<div class=\"formula-card-header\">\n<span class=\"formula-icon\">📐</span>\n<span class=\"formula-title\">Vector Magnitude Formula</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"formula-body\">\n<div class=\"formula-display\">\n\n$$|\\vec{A}| = \\sqrt{A_x^2 + A_y^2 + A_z^2}$$\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"formula-legend\">\n<div class=\"legend-row\">\n<span class=\"legend-symbol\">$$|\\vec{A}|$$</span>\n<span class=\"legend-desc\">Magnitude (scalar value) of vector <strong>A</strong></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"legend-row\">\n<span class=\"legend-symbol\">$$A_x, A_y, A_z$$</span>\n<span class=\"legend-desc\">Components along x, y, z axes</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"formula-note\">\n💡 Notice: the result of this formula is a <em>scalar</em> — magnitude has no direction.\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<div class=\"concept-card full-width\">\n<div class=\"card-header key-header\">\n<span class=\"card-icon\">⚡</span>\n<span class=\"card-title\">Key Conceptual Difference — Speed vs Velocity</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"comparison-scenario\">\n<div class=\"scenario-box\">\n<div class=\"scenario-label scalar-label\">SCALAR</div>\n<div class=\"scenario-content\">\n<strong>Speed = 60 km/h</strong><br/>\nTells you <em>how fast</em> — nothing more.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"scenario-arrow\">≠</div>\n<div class=\"scenario-box\">\n<div class=\"scenario-label vector-label\">VECTOR</div>\n<div class=\"scenario-content\">\n<strong>Velocity = 60 km/h North</strong><br/>\nTells you <em>how fast</em> AND <em>where to</em>.\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"scenario-note\">A car going East at 60 km/h and a car going West at 60 km/h have the <strong>same speed</strong> but <strong>opposite velocities</strong>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<div class=\"table-card\">\n<div class=\"card-header table-header\">\n<span class=\"card-icon\">📊</span>\n<span class=\"card-title\">Comparison Table</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\">\n<table class=\"styled-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Property</th>\n<th>Scalar</th>\n<th>Vector</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Definition</td>\n<td>Magnitude only</td>\n<td>Magnitude + Direction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Symbol</td>\n<td>A</td>\n<td><strong>A</strong> or Ā</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Addition Rule</td>\n<td>Simple arithmetic</td>\n<td>Triangle / Parallelogram law</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Division</td>\n<td>Always possible</td>\n<td>Not defined between vectors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Effect of direction</td>\n<td>No effect</td>\n<td>Completely changes the quantity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Example pair</td>\n<td>Distance</td>\n<td>Displacement</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<div class=\"section-grid two-col\">\n\n<div class=\"concept-card\">\n<div class=\"card-header note-header\">\n<span class=\"card-icon\">📝</span>\n<span class=\"card-title\">Important Note</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<p>Some quantities appear similar but belong to different categories:</p>\n<ul class=\"styled-list\">\n<li><strong>Distance</strong> (scalar) vs <strong>Displacement</strong> (vector)</li>\n<li><strong>Speed</strong> (scalar) vs <strong>Velocity</strong> (vector)</li>\n<li><strong>Mass</strong> (scalar) vs <strong>Weight</strong> (vector)</li>\n<li><strong>Energy</strong> (scalar) vs <strong>Force</strong> (vector)</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"concept-card\">\n<div class=\"card-header summary-header\">\n<span class=\"card-icon\">✅</span>\n<span class=\"card-title\">Quick Memory Rule</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"memory-rule\">\n<div class=\"rule-box\">\n<span class=\"rule-icon\">🔢</span>\n<div>\n<strong>Scalar</strong><br/>\nAsk: <em>\"How much?\"</em><br/>\nOne number answers it fully.\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"rule-box\">\n<span class=\"rule-icon\">➡️</span>\n<div>\n<strong>Vector</strong><br/>\nAsk: <em>\"How much AND which way?\"</em><br/>\nDirection is non-negotiable.\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n<style>\n.tutor-response {\n  font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;\n  max-width: 900px;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 8px;\n  color: #1a1a2e;\n}\n\n.section-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 16px;\n  margin: 16px 0;\n}\n\n.two-col {\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 640px) {\n  .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n}\n\n.full-width {\n  grid-column: 1 / -1;\n}\n\n/* === CARDS === */\n.concept-card, .formula-card, .table-card {\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\n  background: #ffffff;\n  border: 1px solid #e8ecf0;\n}\n\n.card-header {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 10px;\n  padding: 12px 18px;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 0.95rem;\n  letter-spacing: 0.3px;\n}\n\n.card-icon { font-size: 1.1rem; }\n.card-title { font-size: 1rem; }\n\n.card-body {\n  padding: 16px 18px;\n  font-size: 0.93rem;\n  line-height: 1.7;\n}\n\n/* Header Colors */\n.intro-header   { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea, #764ba2); color: white; }\n.scalar-header  { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #11998e, #38ef7d); color: white; }\n.vector-header  { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fc4a1a, #f7b733); color: white; }\n.key-header     { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4776E6, #8E54E9); color: white; }\n.table-header   { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e, #16213e); color: white; }\n.note-header    { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f093fb, #f5576c); color: white; }\n.summary-header { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f9b58, #00bf8f); color: white; }\n.formula-card-header { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2c3e50, #4ca1af); color: white; }\n\n/* === PROPERTY LIST === */\n.property-list {\n  background: #f8f9ff;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  margin: 12px 0;\n}\n\n.property-item {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  padding: 5px 0;\n  border-bottom: 1px dashed #e0e4ef;\n  font-size: 0.88rem;\n}\n\n.property-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }\n.property-label { color: #666; font-weight: 500; }\n.property-value { font-weight: 600; color: #1a1a2e; }\n\n/* === EXAMPLE BOXES === */\n.example-box {\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 12px 14px;\n  margin-top: 12px;\n}\n\n.scalar-example { background: #e8fdf5; border-left: 4px solid #11998e; }\n.vector-example { background: #fff4e6; border-left: 4px solid #fc4a1a; }\n\n.example-title {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 0.82rem;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n  color: #555;\n}\n\n.example-tags {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 6px;\n}\n\n.tag {\n  background: white;\n  border: 1px solid #ddd;\n  border-radius: 20px;\n  padding: 3px 10px;\n  font-size: 0.82rem;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  color: #333;\n}\n\n/* === FORMULA CARD === */\n.formula-card-header {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 10px;\n  padding: 12px 18px;\n  font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n.formula-icon { font-size: 1.1rem; }\n.formula-title { font-size: 1rem; }\n\n.formula-body {\n  padding: 20px 24px;\n}\n\n.formula-display {\n  background: #0f1923;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 20px;\n  text-align: center;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n  font-size: 1.3rem;\n}\n\n.formula-legend {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 8px;\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n}\n\n.legend-row {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 14px;\n  font-size: 0.88rem;\n}\n\n.legend-symbol {\n  min-width: 110px;\n  background: #f0f4ff;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  padding: 4px 8px;\n  text-align: center;\n  font-family: monospace;\n}\n\n.legend-desc { color: #444; }\n\n.formula-note {\n  background: #fffbea;\n  border-left: 4px solid #f0c040;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  font-size: 0.88rem;\n  color: #5a4500;\n}\n\n/* === COMPARISON SCENARIO === */\n.comparison-scenario {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 16px;\n  margin: 12px 0;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n\n.scenario-box {\n  flex: 1;\n  min-width: 160px;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 14px;\n  background: #f8f9ff;\n  border: 1px solid #e0e4ef;\n}\n\n.scenario-label {\n  font-size: 0.72rem;\n  font-weight: 800;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  padding: 2px 8px;\n  display: inline-block;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.scalar-label { background: #d4f8ec; color: #0a6e4e; }\n.vector-label { background: #fde8d8; color: #8b2500; }\n\n.scenario-arrow {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  font-weight: 900;\n  color: #cc3333;\n}\n\n.scenario-note {\n  background: #f0f4ff;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  font-size: 0.88rem;\n  margin-top: 10px;\n  color: #333;\n}\n\n/* === TABLE === */\n.table-wrapper {\n  overflow-x: auto;\n  padding: 0 4px 4px;\n}\n\n.styled-table {\n  width: 100%;\n  border-collapse: collapse;\n  font-size: 0.88rem;\n}\n\n.styled-table th {\n  background: #1a1a2e;\n  color: white;\n  padding: 11px 14px;\n  text-align: left;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  letter-spacing: 0.3px;\n}\n\n.styled-table td {\n  padding: 10px 14px;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #eef0f5;\n  color: #333;\n}\n\n.styled-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #f8f9ff; }\n.styled-table tr:hover td { background: #eef2ff; transition: background 0.2s; }\n\n/* === STYLED LIST === */\n.styled-list {\n  padding-left: 18px;\n  margin: 8px 0;\n}\n\n.styled-list li {\n  padding: 4px 0;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n}\n\n/* === MEMORY RULE === */\n.memory-rule {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 12px;\n}\n\n.rule-box {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: flex-start;\n  gap: 12px;\n  background: #f8f9ff;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  font-size: 0.88rem;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n.rule-icon { font-size: 1.4rem; }\n\nhr {\n  border: none;\n  border-top: 1px solid #eef0f5;\n  margin: 8px 0;\n}\n</style>",
